<title>SWEDEN: Skanska says wins $129 mln U.S. order.</title>
<headline>Skanska says wins $129 mln U.S. order.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish construction group Skanska said on Monday its subisidiary company Karl Koch had won an order worth $129 million in the U.S. in partnership with New York company NAB.  </p>
<p>&quot;The contract covers renovation of the Williamsburg Bridge, a suspension bridge between Manhattan and Brooklyn in New York,&quot; Skanska said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company said work will begin this year but most of the work will be done late in 1998 and 1999.</p>
<p>-- Belinda Goldsmith, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1045</p>
